<include>
  <!--
    inbound_ai_dialplan.xml  (TEMPLATE — contains placeholders, do NOT deploy as-is)
    Routes inbound calls from COMtrexx to the Python AI call handler.

    This file is a TEMPLATE. The socket destination is parameterised with the
    placeholders {{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_HOST}} and {{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT}} so the
    same source works across local WSL, Windows portproxy, and Docker/Linux
    deployments without committing a host-specific IP to the repository.

    DO NOT `cp` this file directly into FreeSWITCH — the placeholders would
    break the dialplan. Render it first.

    RENDER + DEPLOY TO (WSL2 Debian12):
      bash backend/voice/freeswitch/render_inbound_dialplan.sh --reload
      # renders to /etc/freeswitch/dialplan/public/00_inbound_ai.xml and reloads

    The renderer substitutes the placeholders from (first match wins):
      AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_HOST  ->  FREESWITCH_ESL_OUTBOUND_HOST  ->  127.0.0.1
      AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT  ->  FREESWITCH_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT  ->  8085

    The FS external profile routes to the "public" context (not "default").
    Inbound calls from gateways always land in "public".

    APPLY WITH (in fs_cli), after rendering:
      reloadxml

    HOW IT WORKS:
      When a call arrives from COMtrexx, FreeSWITCH connects back to the Python
      app on the ESL outbound socket.  Python answers, plays TTS, records
      speech, runs Whisper + LLM, and hangs up.

    NOTE: sip_gateway_name is NOT set for inbound calls (only outbound).
    We match destination_number instead — catches all calls to this FS instance.
    To restrict to a specific extension add:
      expression="^003010$"
  -->
  <extension name="ai_inbound_comtrexx" continue="false">
    <condition field="destination_number" expression="^(.*)$">
      <action application="set"    data="hangup_after_bridge=true"/>
      <action application="set"    data="continue_on_fail=false"/>
      <!--
        {{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_HOST}} = address FreeSWITCH uses to reach the Python
                                    backend's ESL outbound listener. Rendered by
                                    render_inbound_dialplan.sh:
                                      - local WSL (FS+Python same host): 127.0.0.1
                                      - Windows portproxy (Python on Windows): the
                                        host/LAN IP the portproxy forwards from
                                      - Docker/Linux: the backend container/host IP
        {{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT}} = FREESWITCH_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT (default 8085).
        async full               = full event stream, non-blocking dialplan thread.
      -->
      <action application="socket" data="{{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_HOST}}:{{AI_ESL_OUTBOUND_PORT}} async full"/>
    </condition>
  </extension>
</include>
